# Generated API surface snapshot. Prettier reformats the TypeScript inside its fenced
# code blocks — double quotes to single, reindenting members — which made the committed
# baseline disagree with what `api-surface.mjs` produces on every single commit, since
# lint-staged formats `*.md`. The first commit after adding the gate silently corrupted
# it: 476 lines "changed", none of them a real API change.
#
# It is generated output that says "Do not edit by hand" in its own header, so the byte
# comparison has to be against the generator, not against prettier's opinion of it.
/docs/api/platform.api.md

# Storybook's MDX pages. Prettier parses MDX 1, where a blank line ends a JSX block; Storybook 9
# compiles MDX 3, where it does not. So a blank line inside a `<Source code={`…`} />` sample
# ends the block for Prettier, which then re-flows the rest of the sample as Markdown and strips
# its indentation — it did to ten samples, three on Getting started. `{/* prettier-ignore */}`
# covers only the part before the blank line, and Prettier's ignore ranges need HTML comments,
# which MDX 3 rejects.
*.mdx

# Three documents prettier has never formatted — and must not, for the same reason as the API
# snapshot above: it rewrites what is inside their fenced code blocks. In the two i18n documents
# the samples are quoted from real files, and prettier turns `'source':` into `"source":`, so the
# YAML printed in the plan stops matching the `crowdin-conf.yml` it is quoting, and the
# TypeScript sample in the status page stops matching a single-quote codebase. The charter is
# worse: its section headings are bare `1. Overview` / `2. Pre-Requisites` lines, which prettier
# reads as ordered-list items and then indents every following paragraph into, restructuring the
# whole document. All three were already unformatted when this entry was added; staging any of
# them without it silently rewrites far more than the edit.
/README.charter.md
/docs/i18n-localization-plan.md
/docs/i18n-status.md
